1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,890
You can't read with the corner of your eye?

2
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,860
Look only at the yellow dot in the middle

3
00:00:07,910 --> 00:00:11,410
Without moving your eyes,
try to read the words on both sides

4
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:16,180
Eyes on the dot — what are the side words?

5
00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:20,180
Keep your eyes in the middle!

6
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:22,150
Answer: 고래 (whale) · 딸기 (strawberry)

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,720
Hard to read
without moving your eyes, right?

8
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:27,790
If we spread out the inner wall
of the eye (the retina)

9
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:29,760
The cells for letters and color
are packed only in the very center

10
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:33,130
The edges have cells
for darkness and movement

11
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:36,900
The sharp spot is only as big as
your thumbnail at arm's length!

12
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:41,350
So your eyes jump around
several times a second to read

13
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,320
Have a friend slowly bring a colored pencil
in from the side

14
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:48,720
You notice the movement first
and the color later

15
00:00:48,770 --> 00:00:50,770
You never noticed
because your eyes are always busy moving!

16
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:53,270
NEXT: A sausage floating between two fingers?
